From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: use source IP flow keys

The flow insertion command hashes entries by source IP regardless of the
packet direction.  Boot firmware can leave one or more FLOW_CTRL1 key
selectors set, making the corresponding direction use the destination IP
for lookup instead.  Such entries are accepted by the hardware but never
match packets; on IPQ5332 this was observed as 0x00020000 in both unicast
FLOW_CTRL1 rows and zero packet counters under sustained traffic.

Clear every unicast key selector for both IPv4 and IPv6 so lookup uses the
same source-IP key as insertion in every direction.  Leave the multicast
row untouched.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flow.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flow.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flow.c
@@ -639,7 +639,7 @@ int ppe_nexthop_set(struct ppe_device *p
 int ppe_flow_hw_init(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev)
 {
 	u32 mask, val;
-	int ret;
+	int type, ret;
 
 	mutex_init(&ppe_dev->flow_lock);
 
@@ -649,6 +649,17 @@ int ppe_flow_hw_init(struct ppe_device *
 	 */
 	ppe_dev->flow_cmd_id = 1;
 
+	/* Flow insertion hashes on the source address for both directions.
+	 * Match lookup to it instead of inheriting firmware key selection.
+	 */
+	for (type = 0; type < 2; type++) {
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(ppe_dev->regmap,
+					 PPE_FLOW_CTRL1_ADDR + type * PPE_FLOW_CTRL1_INC,
+					 PPE_FLOW_CTRL1_KEY_SEL, 0);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	mask = PPE_L3_ROUTE_CTRL_IP_MRU_FAIL |
 	       PPE_L3_ROUTE_CTRL_IP_MRU_DEACCEL |
 	       PPE_L3_ROUTE_CTRL_IP_MTU_FAIL |
